# Pre-commit Hooks

This project uses [pre-commit](https://pre-commit.com) to run code quality checks
automatically before every `git commit`. No check needs to be run manually — they fire on
`git commit` and block the commit if any hook fails.

---

## Installation

```bash
pip install pre-commit
pre-commit install
```

After `pre-commit install`, every future `git commit` will trigger the configured hooks.
To run all hooks manually on the entire codebase (without committing):

```bash
pre-commit run --all-files
```

To run a single hook by id:

```bash
pre-commit run <hook-id> --all-files
```

---

## Updating hook versions

Hook revisions are pinned in `.pre-commit-config.yaml`. To upgrade all hooks to their
latest versions:

```bash
pre-commit autoupdate
```

---

## Hygiene hooks (always active)

These run on every commit regardless of which optional tools you selected.

| Hook | What it does |
|------|--------------|
| `trailing-whitespace` | Removes trailing spaces and tabs from every line |
| `end-of-file-fixer` | Ensures every file ends with exactly one newline |
| `check-added-large-files` | Blocks commits that accidentally add large binary files |
| `check-merge-conflict` | Prevents committing files that still contain merge conflict markers (`<<<<<<`, `>>>>>>`) |
| `mixed-line-ending` | Normalises line endings — prevents CRLF/LF mixing |
| `check-ast` | Parses every `.py` file and errors if the syntax is invalid Python |
| `debug-statements` | Blocks commits that contain `pdb`, `ipdb`, `breakpoint()`, etc. |
| `check-yaml` | Validates YAML files are well-formed |
| `check-toml` | Validates TOML files (including `pyproject.toml`) |
{% if "detect-secrets" in optional_deps %}
| `detect-aws-credentials` | Scans for accidentally committed AWS key patterns |
{% endif %}

